## Implemented: `hmloader` + `.hmmod` precompiled mod format

Forked upstream to https://github.com/promikailamin/horizon and added the mod loader in this repository.

### What was built

- **`.hmmod` format 1**: deterministic ZIP with `hmmod.json`, per-file SHA-256, Horizon revision/target/profile pins, the prebuilt `horizon-client`, and the original `.hnmod` source under `source/` for transparency.
- **`hmloader` CLI**: `info`, `install`, `list`, `remove`, `verify`, `launch`, `convert`, `pack`, `import-launcher`, `doctor`.
- **Converter**: stages the pinned Horizon source with `horizon-mixins`, applies one or more `.hnmod` bundles, compiles `horizon-client` once on the author machine, and packages it. Players install/launch without Rust or Cargo.
- **Safety checks**: path traversal, symlinks, duplicate files, unknown files and checksum mismatches are rejected. Only the declared client gets `0755`.
- **Official launcher integration**: `import-launcher` imports the prebuilt client as its own launcher version via the official `import-build` path.
- **Docs**: full beginner-to-advanced README, format spec and validation report.

### Tests actually run

- Downloaded official Horizon launcher `0.2.67`; installed `nightly-2026-11-13-9f42064`; verified its native-build correctly refuses because resources are unprepared.
- Converted the included test `.hnmod` (`example_mod-0.1.0.hnmod`, Horizon `ba6344a…`, horizon-mixins `d9c83d7…`) **end-to-end with a full compile** (~5m42s), no prebuilt-binary shortcut.
- Installed, listed, verified and launched the resulting `.hmmod`; the prebuilt modded client printed its Horizon 26.3 `--help`.
- Confirmed the mod is inside the binary: `[example_mod] Breaking block at`.
- Confirmed deterministic output: two conversions produced the same SHA-256.
- Imported the build into the official launcher (`imported-2026-11-15-1efd64d`) and confirmed it was selected.
- `cargo fmt`, `cargo clippy -D warnings`, and 5/5 tests pass.

### Release

https://github.com/promikailamin/horizon_modloader/releases/tag/hmloader-v0.1.0

- `hmloader-x86_64-unknown-linux-gnu` — SHA-256 `c6c466fb2a4db699688b59b339d022fd53f01a2b7d8753a80092dd293a4d8bfd`
- `example_mod-0.1.0.hmmod` — SHA-256 `a628e32cc4623b9e7afce722b4b2bf686e69c47da57d77574ea54ad114fdd7c9`
- `SHA256SUMS`

Both release assets were downloaded again and hashes matched.

### Important limitation / remaining problem

Horizon native mods are compile-time source mixins, not runtime plugins. There is no stable hook ABI for arbitrary `.so`/`.dll` mods, so an `.hmmod` carries a complete prebuilt client. Multiple mods must be converted **together** into one `.hmmod` (the converter supports this). A true small-plugin loader would require an upstream Horizon runtime-hook ABI.

Interactive gameplay was not run in CI: the runner has no Microsoft account that owns Minecraft and no legally prepared Minecraft 26.3 resources. Install, verification, launch and client startup were verified; world rendering needs those private resources.

Commits: `ac04ec7`, `571a072`, `982b5f3`, `5f825a0` on `main`. Full logs in `.agent-work/logs/` and `.agent-work/outputs/SHA256SUMS`.
