Horizon's .hnmod files are compiled on every player's computer. hmloader installs .hmmod files, which already contain the compiled Horizon client, and starts it without a Rust build.

Usage: hmloader [OPTIONS] <COMMAND>

Commands:
  info             Show what an .hmmod contains, without installing it
  install          Verify, unpack and add an .hmmod to the mods folder
  list             List installed mods
  remove           Remove an installed mod and its unpacked files
  verify           Check hashes, target and the unpacked client of an installed mod
  launch           Launch the prebuilt Horizon client of an installed mod
  install-dir      Install every .hmmod directly inside a folder
  runtime          Drop-in runtime loader: install a mod folder, then start a build that contains every installed mod
  combine          Combine a folder of .hmmod files into one package using the original .hnmod sources they carry. Needs a Rust build environment
  convert          Convert one or more .hnmod bundles into one precompiled .hmmod
  pack             Package an already-built horizon-client as an .hmmod (advanced/testing)
  import-launcher  Ask the official Horizon launcher to import a precompiled client as a version
  doctor           Check the environment and installed mods
