Implemented and pushed to `main` (commits `466b983`, `da30c56`, `0c0f16c`).

- Added `hmloader runtime [dir]`, `install-dir`, and `combine` for drop-in mod folders and combining separately built `.hmmod` files from their embedded `.hnmod` sources.
- Added portable loader packaging plus the **Build runtime loader** workflow for Linux, Windows, and macOS.
- Added `docs/RUNTIME_LOADER.md`, README/release notes, safety checks, and 15 tests.
- `cargo fmt`, `cargo clippy -D warnings`, `cargo test`, and `actionlint` passed.

True Fabric-style runtime plugin loading remains impossible without an upstream Horizon plugin ABI, since `.hmmod` contains a whole compiled client. The issue was updated: https://github.com/promikailamin/horizon_modloader/issues/7#issuecomment-6905912477
